    {
      "id": "ab433e97-8d5a-4d7e-84a0-77abbeda3863",
      "name": "Why MCP is the Future of AI Integrations",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Why MCP is the Future of AI Integrations",
      "docTypeId": "825bc3cc-9c37-4ec1-b395-9d2ed883c5ba",
      "templateId": null,
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "Why MCP is the Future of AI Integrations"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "featuredImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "9a6bc700-7d8f-49e5-97e1-2a5d72d84b6a",
              "mediaKey": "9a6bc700-7d8f-49e5-97e1-2a5d72d84b6a",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "Model-Context Protocol simplifies how AI systems communicate with applications. Learn why it's becoming the standard for AI integration."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "content",
          "value": {
            "markup": "<h2>The Evolution of AI Communication</h2><p>Model-Context Protocol (MCP) represents a paradigm shift in how AI systems interact with applications. Instead of building custom integrations for every tool, MCP provides a standardized way for AI assistants to access and manipulate data across different systems.</p><h2>Key Benefits</h2><p><strong>Standardization:</strong> One protocol works across all AI implementations and applications. No more one-off integrations.</p><p><strong>Security:</strong> Built-in authentication and authorization mechanisms ensure that AI systems can only access what they're permitted to access.</p><p><strong>Extensibility:</strong> New tools and data sources can be added through simple server implementations without changing the AI application itself.</p><p><strong>Efficiency:</strong> Reduces development time and maintenance overhead significantly.</p><h2>Real-World Applications</h2><p>From document management to project planning, MCP enables AI to seamlessly integrate with your existing workflows. It's transforming how teams work with artificial intelligence across their entire technology stack.</p>",
            "blocks": {
              "layout": {},
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": []
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "urls": [
        "/why-mcp-is-the-future-of-ai-integrations/"
      ],
      "docType": "blogPost",
      "template": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7314d2a3-734c-4fa5-8f90-afd91fbf222f",
      "name": "Getting Started with MCP: A Developer's Guide",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Getting Started with MCP: A Developer's Guide",
      "docTypeId": "825bc3cc-9c37-4ec1-b395-9d2ed883c5ba",
      "templateId": null,
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "Getting Started with MCP: A Developer's Guide"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "featuredImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "77b3687f-0c07-4452-b1f3-586192009d01",
              "mediaKey": "77b3687f-0c07-4452-b1f3-586192009d01",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "A practical guide to implementing Model-Context Protocol in your applications. Learn the basics and start building MCP servers today."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "content",
          "value": {
            "markup": "<h2>What You Need to Know</h2><p>Model-Context Protocol is designed to be simple to implement while powerful in what it enables. Whether you're building a new application or integrating with existing systems, MCP provides a clean, standardized interface.</p><h2>Getting Started</h2><p><strong>Step 1: Understand the Basics</strong> - MCP uses a client-server architecture where applications (clients) request tools and resources from servers.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Choose Your Stack</strong> - MCP SDKs are available in multiple languages. Pick the one that matches your technology.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Define Your Tools</strong> - Think about what capabilities your server should expose to AI clients.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Implement and Test</strong> - Build your server and integrate it with AI applications to start seeing the benefits.</p><h2>Best Practices</h2><p>Start small with a single tool or resource. Test thoroughly with different AI systems. Document your tools clearly. Version your API carefully to maintain compatibility. Monitor usage and iterate based on feedback.</p><h2>Next Steps</h2><p>Join the growing community of developers building with MCP. Share your implementations and learn from others. The protocol is still evolving, and your feedback helps shape its future.</p>",
            "blocks": {
              "layout": {},
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": []
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "urls": [
        "/getting-started-with-mcp-a-developers-guide/"
      ],
      "docType": "blogPost",
      "template": null
    }
